<title>USA: PECO Pa. nuclear unit at 64 pct power - NRC.</title>
<headline>PECO Pa. nuclear unit at 64 pct power - NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>PECO Energy Co's 1,100 megawatt Peach Bottom 2 nuclear power unit in Delta, Pa., is operating at 64 percent power, Nuclear Regulatory Commission said in its Tuesday morning report.</p>
<p>NRC attributed the power reduction to a &quot;control rod pattern adjustment.&quot;</p>
<p>Monday, the company said the unit returned to 100 percent power after being shut last Wednesday due to a problem with the oil line to the generator.</p>
<p>The company was not available for comment.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk 212-859-1628</p>
